enslaved people in St. James Parish and several other specific localities in the southern United States. Proclamation 
No. 95, Regarding the Status of Slaves in States Engaged in Rebellion Against the United States (Jan. 1, 1863). 
Louisiana did not formally abolish slavery in these localities until 1864. Complaint, supra note 15, at 20-22. 
32 FORENSIC ARCHITECTURE, ENVIRONMENTAL RACISM IN DEATH ALLEY, LOUISIANA PHASE I INVESTIGATIVE 
